From 8172c9dc96aafad87baa088802c42db06d1e6279 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan <kloterstefan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 06:52:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] Vizzbox 1.1: favourites with sounds
 (BRIEF-VIZZBOX-1.1.md 3.9)

SAVE + a white key keeps, besides the song, what the user took: a track's sound (a factory preset by engine and
preset, a user sound by its slot: what lies there when loaded plays), its eight parameters turned last, the buses.
Loading puts them back as the user's (a track the favourite holds gets its sound and values in place of what the
user had there; the others stay). A favourite with nothing taken is as in 1.0. In the favourites' own sectors after
the record the Vizzbox 1.0 reads (VB_XOFF 0x100): an entry each with the song it goes with and a CRC of its own, so
the 1.0 reads its songs as before, and a favourite it saves over loses only its own sounds. Written with the record,
while stopped. The GLO layer's list marks them with a +.

Tests: producer_test fav_sounds (saved, a fresh device booting on that flash in a process of its own, loaded, over a
new style; the eight latest; a favourite with nothing taken; a slot with another sound now), vizzbox_compat with the
Vizzbox 1.0's tree both ways (each old tree now with its own tests/hostsim.c), two faults more in the counter-check.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R1rawochSWXFaES57pjc4r
